# AI Memory System (memory-kit) Protocol

This project (FAOPS / Q9 Multi-Speciality Hospital site) uses an audit-enforced,
bidirectional, linked-memory system located in the `ai-context/` directory,
anchored by `CLAUDE.md` at the project root. You MUST strictly adhere to this
memory system.

## 1. Context Loading on Session Start (MANDATORY)

Before writing any code, executing scripts, or suggesting architecture decisions,
you MUST read the following context nodes to understand the project state:

- `CLAUDE.md` -- The root memory node (overall workspace rules and role definition).
- `ai-context/state.md` -- Current active tasks, blockers, and module status
  (max 100 lines).
- `ai-context/modules/<module>/<module>.md` -- The specific context file for
  whichever module/feature area you are touching (max 250 lines).

Module map (pick the ones touching your change):

- `routing-shell`          -- `src/App.jsx`, `src/main.jsx`, `src/layout/MainLayout.jsx`, `src/components/ScrollToTop.jsx`
- `navigation`             -- `src/components/layout/*`, `src/components/Footer.jsx`, `src/components/EmergencyBanner.jsx`
- `home`                   -- `src/pages/Home.jsx`, `src/components/Hero.jsx`, `src/components/PresidentMessage.jsx`
- `about-governance`       -- About / History / Vision / Mission / Values / Programs / Council / Committee / Advisory / Organization / GeneralAssembly / Constitution / Presidentcorner + `src/components/about/*`
- `doctors`                -- `src/pages/Doctors.jsx`, `src/pages/DoctorProfile.jsx`, `src/components/DoctorCard.jsx`, `src/data/doctors.js`
- `departments-services`   -- `src/pages/Departments.jsx`, `DepartmentDetails.jsx`, `Services.jsx`, `src/components/DepartmentCard.jsx`, `src/data/department*.js*`
- `appointment`            -- `src/pages/Appointment.jsx`, `src/components/AppointmentForm.jsx`
- `events-congresses`      -- `src/pages/Events.jsx`, `Congresses.jsx`, `SocietyCongresses.jsx`, `src/components/events/*`, `src/data/eventsData.js`
- `membership`             -- `src/pages/MembershipPage.jsx`, `Membership.jsx`, `Countrydetails.jsx`, `src/data/membershipData.js`, `src/data/countryDetailsData.js`
- `gallery-media`          -- `src/pages/Gallery.jsx`, `gallerygrid.jsx`, `FAOPS2022.jsx`, `FAOPS2023.jsx`, `src/components/GalleryGrid.jsx`, `public/gallery/*`
- `publications`           -- `src/pages/Pulication.jsx`, `src/data/publicationsData.js`, `public/*.pdf`
- `contact-faq`            -- `src/pages/Contact.jsx`, `ContactUs.jsx`, `FAQ.jsx`, `UsefulLinks.jsx`, `src/components/FAQItem.jsx`
- `legal`                  -- `src/pages/PrivacyPolicy.jsx`, `TermsConditions.jsx`, `Cookiepolicy.jsx`
- `data-layer`             -- `src/data/*` (all static datasets and nav config)

## 2. Self-Healing & Memory Modification Rules

When you edit files in the codebase, you are responsible for updating the
corresponding memory files:

- **Bumping Verification:** When you create or modify a memory file, bump its
  `last_verified` UTC timestamp in the YAML frontmatter to the current time.
- **Preserving Links:** Maintain the parent-child structure. If you add a new
  memory file, declare its `parent` relative path in the frontmatter, and add it
  to the `children` array of its parent node.
- **Compaction & Size Control:** Keep memory concise.
  - Module memory files must not exceed 250 lines.
  - State files must not exceed 100 lines.
  - If a file starts bloating, prune completed items or archive older logs into
    `ai-context/archive/`.

## 3. Drift Prevention (The Anti-Rot Core)

Any code modification requires a matching memory documentation update.

- If you modify code under a module path (see map above), you MUST update the
  corresponding documentation under `ai-context/modules/<name>/` in the same turn
  or in a follow-up commit.
- Document any schema changes, route additions, data-source changes, or design
  decisions.
- New page under `src/pages/` -> add its route in `routing-shell` memory AND its
  domain module memory. Do not leave routes undocumented.

## 4. Code Grounding (Anchors)

Ground documentation in reality. When adding documentation, link it to specific
source files using YAML frontmatter anchors:

- `code:<file-path>:<line-range>` (e.g. `code:src/App.jsx:1-120`)
- `data:<file-path>` (e.g. `data:src/data/doctors.js`)
- `asset:<file-path>` (e.g. `asset:public/gallery/`)

Prefer citing the source over duplicating its contents inside memory.

## 5. Verification

After completing a task:

- Run `npm run memory:audit` to verify bidirectional links, frontmatter syntax,
  and size caps.
- Run `npm run build` (Vite) to confirm the app still compiles.
- Fix any formatting, linking, or build violations before completing your turn.

Helper scripts:
- `npm run memory:audit`  -- validate links, frontmatter, size caps
- `npm run memory:doctor` -- deeper health check (stale nodes, orphans)
- `npm run memory:new -- <path>` -- scaffold a new memory node with correct frontmatter
